# cairn

Use cairn to get a human's review of a document, image, diagram, or html page. Submit it as an Artifact. The human reads it in a web UI and writes Comments in Threads. Read the Comments and answer them by editing the Artifact. Each edit creates a new Revision.

Commands print JSON on stdout when any of `AI_AGENT`, `CLAUDECODE`, `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT`, or `PI_CODING_AGENT` is set, or when stdout is not a terminal. `get` prints raw content instead. Pass `--json` or set `CAIRN_FORMAT=json` to force JSON. Pass `--text` or set `CAIRN_FORMAT=text` to force text. Errors on stderr follow the same format. JSON errors have a `code` and a `message`. Exit codes are listed under "Exit codes". Run `cairn <command> --help` for the flags of one command.

## Workflow

1. Submit the document. Note the printed ref (`abc123@1`). The Artifact id is the part before `@`.

```sh
cairn submit plan.md
```

2. Tell the human the Artifact id. Wait for Comments. `--wait` blocks until a Comment newer than the highest existing one arrives. Exit 5 means none arrived in time. Run the command again.

```sh
cairn comment list abc123 --wait
```

3. Edit the Artifact. Pass the Revision number you last read as `--base`. Exit 6 means a newer Revision exists. Run `cairn get abc123`, merge your change into it, and retry. Pass the root Comment ids you addressed as `--addresses`. Each named Thread gets the reply "addressed in abc123@2" and stays open for the human to resolve.

```sh
cairn edit abc123 plan.md --base 1 --addresses 12,14
```

4. Note the highest Comment id you have seen. Wait again with `--since` set to that id. Each round returns only new Threads. Repeat from step 3.

```sh
cairn comment list abc123 --since 14 --wait
```

For a large markdown document, edit one Section instead of resending the whole file (see "Section paths"). To comment yourself, run `cairn comment add`. To reply inside a Thread, add `--reply`.

## Choosing a Kind

Cairn infers the Kind from the file extension. When submitting from stdin, pass `--kind` and `--name`.

- `markdown`: prose, plans, specs, reports. Choose it by default. Only markdown has Sections.
- `image`: a picture file. Submit it alone, then embed it in markdown.
- `diagram`: Mermaid (`.mmd`) or SVG source. Pass `--format svg` for SVG. Cairn rejects invalid Mermaid with exit 4.
- `html`: a single `.html` file or a directory with an `index.html`. Use it for an interactive page or a rendered report.

```sh
cairn submit diagram.mmd
cairn submit shot.png
cairn submit - --kind markdown --name notes
```

## Embeds

To show an image or diagram Artifact inside markdown, submit that Artifact first. Then reference its id. Write `![alt](cairn:abc123)` for the latest Revision. Write `![alt](cairn:abc123@2)` to pin a Revision. Use `cairn:` references, because cairn does not upload local file paths. Exit 4 means the embed names a missing Artifact, a missing Revision, or a markdown or html Artifact.

## Section paths

A Section is a markdown heading plus everything under it, children included. Its path joins the heading texts with ` > `, for example `Design > Storage`. Use a suffix of the path when the suffix is unique. Otherwise add `#n` to pick the nth match (`Notes#2`). Escape `\`, `>`, and a `#` before trailing digits in heading text with a backslash (`Issue \#12`, `A \> B`). List the exact paths:

```sh
cairn outline abc123
```

Use a path to read, edit, or comment on one Section:

```sh
cairn get abc123 --section "Design > Storage"
cairn edit abc123 storage.md --section "Design > Storage"
cairn comment add abc123 "Why SQLite?" --section "Design > Storage"
```

Start a replacement file with a heading at the same level as the Section. Use headings at that level or deeper only. An ambiguous or missing path exits 4.

## Link the human to an Artifact

Only the human starts the web UI, by running `cairn serve` in a terminal. Ask them to run it when they cannot open the Artifact. Do not run `cairn serve` yourself, because it never returns. Print the link to an Artifact:

```sh
cairn view abc123
```

The link loads only while `cairn serve` runs. Tell the human to run `cairn serve` when it does not load.

## Reference

### Global flags

Accepted by every command.

- `--role <ROLE>`: Attribution role for this invocation [env: CAIRN_ROLE] [default: agent] [values: agent, reviewer]
- `--author <AUTHOR>`: Author name (default: the role name) [env: CAIRN_AGENT]
- `--session <SESSION>`: Session label (falls back to CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID) [env: CAIRN_SESSION]
- `--db <DB>`: Database path [env: CAIRN_DB]
- `--project <PROJECT>`: Project root path or name (default: detected from the cwd) [env: CAIRN_PROJECT]
- `--json`: Print JSON (the default in agent sessions and when output is not a terminal; env CAIRN_FORMAT=json|text)
- `--text`: Print human-readable text (the default on a terminal outside agent sessions)

### Exit codes

| Code | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | Success |
| 1 | Unexpected error, including database busy past the 5 s timeout |
| 2 | Usage error, including `delete` without `--yes` |
| 3 | Not found, including a write to a deleted Artifact |
| 4 | Rejected input: limits, bad Kind, missing embed target, invalid Mermaid, ambiguous or missing Section |
| 5 | `comment list --wait` timed out with nothing new |
| 6 | Conflict: `edit --base` named a stale Revision |

`cairn skill --check` also exits 1 when the installed skill is stale. In JSON mode errors print `{"code": ..., "message": ...}` on stderr.

### Commands

#### `cairn submit`

Store a new Artifact and print its ref

```
cairn submit [OPTIONS] <PATH>
```

- `<PATH>`: File, directory (an html Bundle) or `-` for stdin
- `--kind <KIND>`: Artifact Kind (inferred from the extension; required for stdin) [values: markdown, html, image, diagram]
- `--name <NAME>`: Artifact name (default: the file name; required for stdin)
- `--format <FORMAT>`: Diagram format (`.mmd` implies mermaid; required for svg and stdin) [values: mermaid, svg]

#### `cairn edit`

Replace an Artifact's content with a new Revision and print its ref

```
cairn edit [OPTIONS] <ID> <PATH>
```

- `<ID>`: Artifact id (no `@revision`)
- `<PATH>`: File, directory (html Bundle) or `-` for stdin
- `--base <BASE>`: Refuse unless this is still the latest Revision (exit 6)
- `--section <SECTION>`: Replace only this markdown Section ("A > B"); the file must start with its heading
- `--addresses <COMMENT_IDS>`: Reply "addressed in <ref>" in these Threads (root comment ids, comma-separated); they stay open

#### `cairn get`

Print an Artifact's content: `abc123` or `abc123@2`

```
cairn get [OPTIONS] <TARGET>
```

- `<TARGET>`: `abc123` or `abc123@2`; defaults to the latest Revision
- `--section <SECTION>`: Print only this markdown Section ("A > B", children included)
- `--out <OUT>`: Directory to write an image or html Artifact's files into, or a diagram's rendered diagram.svg
- `--render`: Print a diagram Artifact as SVG (mermaid is rendered; svg is printed as stored)

#### `cairn view`

Print the web UI URL of an Artifact (`abc123` or `abc123@2`) without checking a server

```
cairn view [OPTIONS] <TARGET>
```

- `<TARGET>`: `abc123` or `abc123@2`
- `--url <URL>`: UI base URL (default: http://127.0.0.1:<CAIRN_PORT or 7878>) [env: CAIRN_URL]

#### `cairn outline`

List a markdown Artifact's headings with their paths and sizes

```
cairn outline <TARGET>
```

- `<TARGET>`: `abc123` or `abc123@2`; defaults to the latest Revision

#### `cairn embeds`

List a markdown Artifact's `cairn:` image embeds, resolved now, with line and alt text

```
cairn embeds <TARGET>
```

- `<TARGET>`: `abc123` or `abc123@2`; defaults to the latest Revision

#### `cairn list`

List Artifacts, newest activity first

```
cairn list [OPTIONS]
```

- `--kind <KIND>`: Only this Kind [values: markdown, html, image, diagram]
- `--mine`: Only Artifacts created by the caller (its Session if it has one, else its author)
- `--open`: Only Artifacts with open Threads
- `--older-than <DURATION>`: Only Artifacts last updated longer ago than this: 30d, 12h, 90m, 45s, 2w
- `--limit <LIMIT>`: Maximum rows [default: 50]
- `--all-projects`: Show Artifacts of every Project
- `--all-worktrees`: Also show Artifacts of every linked worktree of the Project
- `--project-root <PATH>`: Only the Project with this root path (narrows a name shared by several)

#### `cairn comment`

Comments and Threads

```
cairn comment <COMMAND>
```

#### `cairn comment add`

Add a Comment (a new Thread, or a reply with --reply)

```
cairn comment add [OPTIONS] <TARGET> <BODY>
```

- `<TARGET>`: `abc123` or `abc123@2`; defaults to the latest Revision
- `<BODY>`: Comment text, or `-` for stdin
- `--lines <LINES>`: Anchor to a line range of a text Artifact (`a-b` or `a`); the quote is stored
- `--section <SECTION>`: Anchor to a markdown Section ("A > B"), resolved against the Comment's own Revision
- `--reply <COMMENT_ID>`: Reply in the Thread of this root Comment id

#### `cairn comment resolve`

Resolve a Thread

```
cairn comment resolve <THREAD_ID>
```

- `<THREAD_ID>`: Root Comment id of the Thread

#### `cairn comment reopen`

Reopen a resolved Thread

```
cairn comment reopen <THREAD_ID>
```

- `<THREAD_ID>`: Root Comment id of the Thread

#### `cairn comment list`

List Threads (open ones by default, on any Revision, stale included)

```
cairn comment list [OPTIONS] [TARGET]
```

- `[TARGET]`: Only this Artifact (no `@revision`); ignores the Session scope
- `--all`: Include resolved Threads
- `--since <COMMENT_ID>`: Only Threads holding a Comment newer than this id, with all their replies; the open/--all rule still applies
- `--wait`: Block until something newer than --since (default: the highest Comment id now) exists; exit 5 on timeout
- `--timeout <SECS>`: Seconds to wait before giving up [default: 60]
- `--all-projects`: Show Artifacts of every Project
- `--all-worktrees`: Also show Artifacts of every linked worktree of the Project
- `--project-root <PATH>`: Only the Project with this root path (narrows a name shared by several)

#### `cairn delete`

Delete Artifacts with all their Revisions

```
cairn delete [OPTIONS] <IDS>...
```

- `<IDS>...`: Artifact ids
- `--yes`: Confirm the deletion (there is no prompt)
